<h3>2026-08-30 — Director/Coder model configuration</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> Documented and verified the director/coder model role assignment in Hermes Agent configuration. The director role evaluates code/plans and can be any model (grok, deepseek, etc.), while the coder role always uses `nemotron-3.5-lightning-free` (opencode-free) as the reliable free coder for code writing and sub-agents.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> The user wanted the ability to select any model as the director per-task (e.g., grok for AI work, deepseek for data tasks) while keeping the coder/sub-agent always as `nemotron-3.5-lightning-free` for consistency and quota conservation. The delegation configuration (`delegation.model: nemotron-3.5-lightning-free`, `delegation.provider: opencode-free`) ensures the coder stays consistent regardless of which model is active as director.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Fix.</strong> Verified configuration: <br>• `default: grok-composer-2.5-fast` (xai-oauth) — director model <br>• `delegation.model: nemotron-3.5-lightning-free` (opencode-free) — coder model <br>• `fallback_providers` chain of 10 entries shared between director and coder fallback <br>• `director alias: xai-oauth/grok-composer-2.5-fast` <br>• `coder alias: opencode-free/nemotron-3.5-lightning-free` <br>• `Cheap alias: opencode-free/nemotron-3.5-lightning-free` <br>When the configured coder (`nemotron-3.5-lightning-free`) fails, Hermes auto-falls through the shared 10-entry fallback chain. Using `/model <new_model>` switches the director independently of the coder, which remains fixed as `nemotron-3.5-lightning-free`.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>/home/shanta/.hermes/config.yaml</code> (model.aliases, delegation); <code>~/.hermes/skills/autonomous-ai-agents/hermes-agent/references/configuration.md</code> (reference); <code>~/.hermes/skills/autonomous-ai-agents/hermes-agent/references/providers-and-models.md</code></p>
</div>